        "id": "532031",
        "date_added": "2026-11-24 02:16:58",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static RE Analysis (Linux PAM Master-Password Backdoor — pam_master.so):\n- Unstripped ELF64 shared object (master.c, GCC 4.8.5 Red Hat 4.8.5-44 / CentOS 7).\n- Hooks pam_sm_authenticate \u0026 pam_sm_acct_mgmt: is_master() reads a runtime override hash from /etc/.pm (up to 511 B) or falls back to hardcoded SHA-512 crypt hash: $6$cONA0kbmpUGiT1Vt$j7LdoaXFCMA5lr32B/LMOnvY3z7id6CUEfSl9hIl9lH0kSYNIq.NLLLnGJ7lPCuqnQqHwDnzWO19SNzwD8Fgs/ (rejects placeholder 'REPLACE').\n- Verifies password via crypt_r(); if matched and getpwnam(user) exists, marks session via pam_set_data and returns PAM_SUCCESS (0) for silent access to any valid local account (including root), otherwise returns PAM_IGNORE (0x19)."
      }
    ],
